<?xml version="1.0"?>
<robot name="suzanne">
  <!--
    Dynamic Suzanne for PyBullet (same conventions as bunny.urdf).

    GEOMETRY:
    Mesh is uniformly scaled by 1/2.65187 = 0.3770924 so the largest extent (ear to ear, x) is 1 m.
    Scaled extents: 1.000 x 0.720 x 0.604 m. Mesh axes kept as exported from Blender (y up, face toward +z).
    The link frame sits at the true volumetric center of mass; visual/collision <origin> = -scale*COM.

      Mesh-local COM: (0.0000, 0.2207, 0.0455)
      Bbox center:    (0.0000, -0.0156, 0.0220)

    SOLID MODEL:
    The Blender mesh is not closed: the head has two eye-socket holes and the eyes are
    open-backed domes. For the mass properties, all four boundary loops were capped and the
    head and eyes were boolean-unioned (manifold3d) into one watertight solid, so the eye
    region is counted once. Raw-unit volume 1.982607.

    MASS: 1 kg, uniform density.

    INERTIA: about the COM, in the link frame. Signed-tetrahedron integration (Mirtich 1996)
    on the watertight solid, rescaled to m = 1 kg and mesh scale s (inertia ~ s^2 at fixed mass).
    Cross-checked against a winding-number grid integration of the ORIGINAL open mesh
    (no capping, no boolean): volume and all tensor entries agree to < 0.01 %.
    ixy = ixz = 0 by the mesh's left/right mirror symmetry. iyz != 0: the principal axes
    are rotated 36.2 deg about x relative to the mesh axes.

    Principal moments: (0.0358, 0.0381, 0.0465) kg*m^2

    COLLISION: suzanne_collision.obj - CoACD convex decomposition (threshold 0.03), 50 hulls,
    one "o" block per hull. Hulls exceed the solid volume by 2.4 %.

    Load with flags=p.URDF_USE_INERTIA_FROM_FILE, otherwise PyBullet ignores the tensor above.
  -->
  <link name="suzanne">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="1.0"/>
      <inertia ixx="0.03814392" ixy="0.00000000" ixz="0.00000000"
               iyy="0.04277184" iyz="0.00512584"
               izz="0.03952438"/>
    </inertial>

    <visual>
      <origin xyz="0.000000 -0.083223 -0.017163" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="suzanne.obj" scale="0.3770924 0.3770924 0.3770924"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="suzanne_color">
        <color rgba="0.80 0.62 0.45 1.0"/>
      </material>
    </visual>

    <collision>
      <origin xyz="0.000000 -0.083223 -0.017163" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="suzanne_collision.obj" scale="0.3770924 0.3770924 0.3770924"/>
      </geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>
</robot>
